56	// TestConfigLaunchAndCwdLaunchShareOneBrain is the whole defect, end to end, on
57	// a real symlink.
58	//
59	// Two supported ways to start this binary against one repository:
60	//
61	//	a config-file launch  ENTIRE_REPO_ROOT=<absolute path>, what
62	//	                      `mcp --print-config` bakes into a host's MCP entry
63	//	a cwd launch          no ENTIRE_REPO_ROOT, the repository is simply the
64	//	                      working directory
65	//
66	// They used to disagree. The cwd route resolves symlinks (git reports the
67	// physical root; so does the getcwd syscall), while the config route kept
68	// whatever absolute string was printed -- and `--print-config` printed the
69	// UNRESOLVED path, because os.Getwd honours $PWD. So on macOS a repository
70	// under /tmp got one brain per route, and once both existed every repo-scoped
71	// command -- including brain_delete_project, the one that could have cleared
72	// them -- refused with repo_identity_conflict. The MCP surface had no way out.
